1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,418
An impersonator can copy a creator's
photos and

2
00:00:03,418 --> 00:00:08,218
biography while changing just the
username. MirrorCheck helps turn

3
00:00:08,218 --> 00:00:12,000
that suspicion into evidence a reviewer
can inspect.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,905
This is our working, unofficial
Instagram-style web prototype.

5
00:00:17,905 --> 00:00:22,952
These two fictional accounts share a name,
biography,

6
00:00:22,952 --> 00:00:28,000
avatar and post images, but have different
usernames.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,697
From the suspected copy, I choose Report
account, then Pretending

8
00:00:33,697 --> 00:00:37,817
to be someone else. I attach screenshots
of the

9
00:00:37,817 --> 00:00:43,777
original and suspected profile. PaddleOCR
fills editable fields, and

10
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:50,000
I correct the extracted text against the
screenshots before submitting.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,697
Before any image reaches Meta AI, Presidio
identifies the example

12
00:00:55,697 --> 00:01:01,482
email and phone. The server permanently
covers both contact lines.

13
00:01:01,482 --> 00:01:06,653
These previews are the actual processed
images prepared for

14
00:01:06,653 --> 00:01:12,000
Meta, with matching hashes for the
evidence saved for review.

15
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,822
Meta Muse Spark analyzes the processed
screenshots

16
00:01:15,822 --> 00:01:21,019
through our backend and returns structured
similarities, differences

17
00:01:21,019 --> 00:01:24,841
and limitations. Here it identifies reused
profile

18
00:01:24,841 --> 00:01:28,815
content and recommends further review. It
explicitly

19
00:01:28,815 --> 00:01:32,943
says screenshots cannot establish
ownership. This is a

20
00:01:32,943 --> 00:01:36,000
real API response from the recorded run.

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,426
Local models add separate signals: a
text-reuse comparison between the

22
00:01:41,426 --> 00:01:46,388
two profiles, and an auxiliary profile
spam-pattern score. Image

23
00:01:46,388 --> 00:01:51,116
deduplication also finds a matching grid
region. These scores

24
00:01:51,116 --> 00:01:56,000
