or proof of identity.

25
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,247
The report remains Under review. Our
profile model excludes avatar presence,

26
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:08,164
so changing only a default-avatar flag
cannot change its score. The pair

27
00:02:08,164 --> 00:02:14,000
model uses synthetic training data, a
limitation shown to the reviewer.

28
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,340
In the moderator view, I inspect the

29
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:22,258
processed images and analysis, then
explicitly select

30
00:02:22,258 --> 00:02:26,897
Confirm impersonation for this fictional
case. The

31
00:02:26,897 --> 00:02:32,000
AI recommendation alone cannot perform
this transition.

32
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,424
The profile now displays Impersonation
confirmed. Reloading preserves

33
00:02:37,424 --> 00:02:40,961
the warning because the decision is stored
on

34
00:02:40,961 --> 00:02:46,384
the server. This demonstrates the complete
report-to-review workflow;

35
00:02:46,384 --> 00:02:50,000
it does not modify the real Instagram
service.

36
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,355
MirrorCheck makes suspicious copies easier
to review

37
00:02:53,355 --> 00:02:56,000
while reducing contact exposure. Next, we

38
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
need consented real-world evaluation and
production hardening.
